{
  "type": "Pcm16Chunks",
  "description": "Golden vectors for the voice-input audio pipeline shared by the Android, iOS and web clients and asserted against the agent's decoder. Audio is 16 kHz mono PCM16 little-endian; each chunk is uploaded as `pcm16_b64`, standard padded base64 with no line breaks. `chunk_size`: a chunk holds min(sample_rate * 2, max_chunk_bytes) bytes (about one second), rounded down to an even count; null means the agent's limit is too small to carry one sample. `chunk_cases`: `open` lists the chunks sealed while recording is still running (only full chunks), `final` the chunks after the recording stopped (the short tail included, never an empty chunk). A `generator` case builds `count` samples as wrap16(i * multiplier) \u2014 (i * multiplier) mod 65536, minus 65536 when that is 32768 or more \u2014 and pins each chunk by byte length, base64 length and the SHA-256 (hex) of its base64 text. `float_to_pcm16` pins the conversion from Float32 capture buffers (web and iOS; Android records PCM16 directly): non-finite inputs are encoded as the strings \"NaN\", \"Infinity\" and \"-Infinity\".",
  "sample_rate": 16000,
  "chunk_size": [
    {
      "max_chunk_bytes": 65536,
      "chunk_bytes": 32000
    },
    {
      "max_chunk_bytes": 20001,
      "chunk_bytes": 20000
    },
    {
      "max_chunk_bytes": 4096,
      "chunk_bytes": 4096
    },
    {
      "max_chunk_bytes": 1,
      "chunk_bytes": null
    }
  ],
